{"step_index":1280,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:42:14Z","thinking":"**Proving the Roman Dominating Bound**\n\nConsider a Roman dominating function *f* and the set $V_2$ of vertices with value 2. Let *k* be the size of $V_2$. If *k* is zero, then radius + 1 is less or equal to the total weight, as the whole graph is dominated by weight 1 nodes, meaning $|V| \\le W$.\n\nNow considering the case when *k* is 1. It appears that looking at $|V \\setminus B_1(u)| \\le |V_1| = W - 2$ is necessary to establish the bound. Need to analyze how the ball reaches V.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport networkx as nx\nfrom itertools import product\n\n# Find max radius for each value of W = romanWeight(f)\nmax_rad_for_w = {}\nfor n in range(3, 8):\n    for G in nx.graph_atlas_g():\n        if G.number_of_nodes() != n or not nx.is_connected(G):\n            continue\n        rad = nx.radius(G)\n        nodes = list(G.nodes())\n        for f_vals in product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\n            valid = True\n            for i, v in enumerate(nodes):\n                if f_vals[i] == 0:\n                    if not any(f_vals[nodes.index(u)] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)):\n                        valid = False\n                        break\n            if valid:\n                w = sum(f_vals)\n                if w not in max_rad_for_w or rad > max_rad_for_w[w]:\n                    max_rad_for_w[w] = rad\n\nfor w in sorted(max_rad_for_w.keys()):\n    print(f'W = {w}: max radius = {max_rad_for_w[w]}, rad + 1 = {max_rad_for_w[w] + 1}')\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Finding max radius for each W","toolSummary":"Find max radius for each W"}}]}
