{"step_index":1297,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:42:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:42:55+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:42:55+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\nTotal Lines: 537\nTotal Bytes: 27292\nShowing lines 350 to 450\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n350: plain `∀ v a b c : V` binders with `a ≠ b` side conditions: the latter is the\n351: more readable statement (and is what `GraphInvariants.lean` records) but its\n352: `Decidable` instance does not reduce, so `decide` gets stuck on it. This form\n353: reduces. -/\n354: def IsClawFreeClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n355:   ∀ v ∈ (univ : Finset V), ∀ s ∈ univ.powersetCard 3,\n356:     (∀ u ∈ s, G.Adj v u) → ¬ IsIndependentFinset G s\n357: \n358: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n359:     Decidable (IsClawFreeClass G) := by unfold IsClawFreeClass; infer_instance\n360: \n361: /-- Cograph: no four vertices induce a path `P₄`. -/\n362: def IsCographClass (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n363:   ∀ a b c d : V, G.Adj a b → G.Adj b c → G.Adj c d →\n364:     ¬ G.Adj a c → ¬ G.Adj b d → G.Adj a d\n365: \n366: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n367:     Decidable (IsCographClass G) := by unfold IsCographClass; infer_instance\n368: \n369: /- ── sub-total domination ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n370: \n371: /-- Sub-total domination number: least `t` whose `t` largest degrees sum to\n372: `≥ n`.\n373: \n374: graphcalc computes this by sorting the degree sequence and scanning prefixes;\n375: `largestDegreeSum` is that prefix sum expressed as a maximum over `t`-subsets\n376: (see the note there on why sorting is not available to the kernel). -/\n377: def subTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n378:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V) (fun t => Fintype.card V ≤ largestDegreeSum G t)\n379: \n380: /-- Defined exactly when *some* prefix reaches `n`. graphcalc returns no value\n381: when the scan runs off the end — an edgeless graph has every degree `0`, so no\n382: prefix ever reaches `n` — while `minUpTo` would fall back to `n`. Monotonicity\n383: of `largestDegreeSum` makes the whole-graph check `t = n` sufficient. -/\n384: def HasSubTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n385:   Fintype.card V ≤ largestDegreeSum G (Fintype.card V)\n386: \n387: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n388:     Decidable (HasSubTotalDominationNumber G) := by\n389:   unfold HasSubTotalDominationNumber; infer_instance\n390: \n391: /- ── total domination ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n392: \n393: /-- Every vertex has a neighbour in `s` — note `G.Adj v u` excludes `v = u`, so\n394: a vertex may not dominate itself. -/\n395: def IsTotalDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n396:     Prop := ∀ v : V, ∃ u ∈ s, G.Adj v u\n397: \n398: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n399:     Decidable (IsTotalDominatingSet G s) := by\n400:   unfold IsTotalDominatingSet; infer_instance\n401: \n402: def totalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n403:   minCard (IsTotalDominatingSet G)\n404: \n405: /-- Undefined on a graph with an isolated vertex: nothing dominates it, so not\n406: even `univ` is a total dominating set and `minCard` would read `0`. graphcalc\n407: raises there rather than returning a number. -/\n408: def HasTotalDominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n409:   HasWitness (IsTotalDominatingSet G)\n410: \n411: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n412:     Decidable (HasTotalDominationNumber G) := by\n413:   unfold HasTotalDominationNumber; infer_instance\n414: \n415: /- ── edge cover ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n416: \n417: /-- A set of edges meeting every vertex. -/\n418: def IsEdgeCoverFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n419:     (s : Finset (Sym2 V)) : Prop := ∀ v : V, ∃ e ∈ s, v ∈ e\n420: \n421: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset (Sym2 V)) :\n422:     Decidable (IsEdgeCoverFinset G s) := by\n423:   unfold IsEdgeCoverFinset; infer_instance\n424: \n425: /-- Edge cover number: least `k ≤ n` such that some `k` edges meet every vertex.\n426: \n427: Searched by size over `edgeFinset`, not over its whole powerset. A minimum edge\n428: cover never needs more than `n - 1` edges (Gallai: `ρ = n − ν`, and `ν ≥ 1` once\n429: there is an edge), so bounding `k` by `n` loses nothing. It matters: the full\n430: powerset of `K₆`'s 15 edges is 32,768 subsets and exhausted the kernel's\n431: recursion depth, while the subsets of size at most 6 number 9,949. -/\n432: def edgeCoverNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n433:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V)\n434:     (fun k => ∃ s ∈ G.edgeFinset.powersetCard k, IsEdgeCoverFinset G s)\n435: \n436: /-- Undefined exactly when some vertex is isolated — networkx raises \"no edge\n437: cover exists\" there, and `minUpTo`'s fallback would read `n`. An edge cover\n438: exists iff every vertex has a neighbour (take one incident edge per vertex), so\n439: this is stated directly instead of by a second subset search. -/\n440: def HasEdgeCover (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n441:   ∀ v : V, ∃ u : V, G.Adj v u\n442: \n443: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n444:     Decidable (HasEdgeCover G) := by unfold HasEdgeCover; infer_instance\n445: \n446: /- ── Roman domination ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n447: \n448: /-- `f : V → {0,1,2}` is a Roman dominating function when every vertex labelled\n449: `0` has a neighbour labelled `2`.\n450: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
