     by_contra hc\n134:     have h_ssub : ballWithin G (Fintype.card V - 1) v ⊂ Finset.univ :=\n135:       Finset.ssubset_univ_iff.mpr hc\n136:     have h_lt := Finset.card_lt_card h_ssub\n137:     rw [Finset.card_univ] at h_lt\n138:     omega\n139: \n140: lemma eccentricity_le_card_pred {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n141:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\n142:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) :\n143:     GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ≤ Fintype.card V - 1 := by\n144:   unfold GraphCalc.eccentricity\n145:   unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hnt\n146:   unfold GraphCalc.order at hnt\n147:   apply minUpTo_le (Fintype.card V - 1) (by omega) (ballWithin_card_pred_eq_univ G v hrad hnt)\n148: \n149: lemma radius_add_one_le_card {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n150:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n151:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) :\n152:     GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ Fintype.card V := by\n153:   unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hnt\n154:   unfold GraphCalc.order at hnt\n155:   obtain ⟨v⟩ := Fintype.card_pos_iff.mp (by omega : 0 < Fintype.card V)\n156:   have h_rad_le := radius_le_eccentricity G v\n157:   have h_ecc_le := eccentricity_le_card_pred G v hrad hnt\n158:   omega\n159: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":1314,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:43:33Z","thinking":"**Considering Graph Radius Bound**\n\nThe key inequality `radius G + 1 ≤ Fintype.card V` is noted. If `Fintype.card V ≤ romanWeight f`, then `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`. A critical question arises: if `romanWeight f < Fintype.card V`, is it possible that `radius G + 1` is still less than or equal to `romanWeight f`?\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \"\n# If a graph has radius >= 4, can it have a Roman dominating function with weight <= 4?\n# If weight <= 4, then either:\n# 1) weight <= 3 -> we know radius <= 2!\n# 2) weight == 4:\n# What partitions of 4 into {0, 1, 2} exist?\n# 2 + 2: two vertices with label 2, all others 0.\n# 2 + 1 + 1: one vertex with label 2 (unique 2! so radius <= weight - 1 = 3!)\n# 1 + 1 + 1 + 1: four 1s, no 2s! (so |V| <= 4, but radius >= 4 requires |V| >= 8!)\n# So the ONLY partition of weight 4 with radius >= 4 could possibly be 2 + 2!\n# But for 2 + 2:\n# Two vertices u1, u2 have label 2. All other vertices have label 0.\n# So every vertex is adjacent to u1 or u2!\n# That means V = N[u1] U N[u2]!\n# If V = N[u1] U N[u2], what is the maximum possible diameter or radius of G?\n# Let's check: any vertex is at distance <= 1 from {u1, u2}.\n# What is dist(u1, u2)?\n# Since G is connected, either u1 and u2 are adjacent (dist = 1),\n# or they share a neighbor (dist = 2).\n# Wait! Can u1 and u2 be at distance >= 3 if ALL other vertices are in N(u1) U N(u2)?\n# If all other vertices are in N(u1) U N(u2), any path between u1 and u2 MUST go through their neighbors!\n# If there is a path, there is some vertex in N(u1) and some in N(u2) that are connected.\n# If they are the SAME vertex, dist(u1, u2) = 2!\n# If there is an edge between x in N(u1) and y in N(u2), dist(u1, u2) = 3!\n# Could dist(u1, u2) be 4? Only if x and y are connected by another vertex z! But z must also be in N(u1) or N(u2)!\n# So dist(u1, u2) is AT MOST 3!\n# And if dist(u1, u2) <= 3, every vertex is at distance <= 1 from {u1, u2}.\n# Therefore, for ANY vertex x, dist(x, u1) <= 1 + 3 = 4, but what is the RADIUS?!\n# If dist(u1, u2) <= 2: eccentricity(u1) <= 2 + 1 = 3! So radius <= 3!\n# If dist(u1, u2) == 3: say u1 - x - y - u2.\n# Then for vertex x: dist(x, u1) = 1, dist(x, u2) = 2.\n# Any vertex in N[u1] is at distance <= 2 from x!\n# Any vertex in N[u2] is at distance <= 3 from x!\n# So eccentricity(x) <= 3!\n# Therefore RADIUS IS AT MOST 3!\nprint('MATHEMATICAL FACT: If weight(f) <= 4, then radius(G) <= 3 ALWAYS!')\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Analyzing weight 4 radius bound","toolSummary":"Check if weight <= 4 implies radius <= 3"}}]}
